  "goal": "Plan and execute an AIOS-body single-user distribution candidate from RC19 local consumer readiness without giving authority to external mirror frontend, Nginx/TLS, remote signer, object storage, remote dispatch, private signing material, support upload, recovery execution, host boot state, production rings, TUI projections, shell output, endpoint reachability, or model replay.",
  "core_thesis": "AIOS becomes closer to an Ubuntu-like distributable OS when the installable image local consumer chain is packaged as a canonical single-user release bundle with local channel promotion, installer selection, acceptance install, update, rollback, and support/recovery closure evidence, while host and production authority remain untouched.",
  "non_goals": [
